# commontrace-v2 — environment variable reference
#
# Copy to .env and fill in real values, OR export these directly in your shell.
# .env is already covered by .gitignore — never commit a filled-in copy.
#
# This file documents every environment variable the codebase actually reads
# today. It intentionally does NOT include Hub API keys/endpoints: the Hub
# server does not exist in this repository yet (see protocol/PROTOCOL.md §5 —
# `commontrace sync` currently only prints instructions, it makes no network
# call), so there is nothing real for the client to read a credential for.
# When a Hub client ships, its connection variables belong here.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Path resolution (optional — everything auto-detects without these)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Root of the commontrace installation. Only needed if a script is run from a
# location other than inside the checkout/install directory it should operate
# on (e.g. a cron job, a symlinked script). See README.md "Configuration".
# COMMONTRACE_ROOT=/opt/commontrace

# Legacy alias for COMMONTRACE_ROOT, kept for backward compatibility with
# pre-rename (justdoit) installs. Prefer COMMONTRACE_ROOT for new setups.
# JUSTDOIT_ROOT=/opt/commontrace
